window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y3v3-index"]=[{"i":"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p12-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru shiina-hiyori","q":"shiina hiyori depth review  the unspoken confession seaside monologue before the exam  hiyori looks out at the ocean  alone   i am sorry  ryuuen kun   please forgive me for being so pathetic  speaks in apologetic  self effacing terms toward both ryuen and ayanokoji  keeps her feelings to herself   admits she never said  i like you  because they are now enemies  resolves to defeat ayanokoji so class d can reach class a  sees the exam as  a path to survival and a path to death at the same time  vows to inflict defeat on him while her feelings remain unchanged  apologises to him for not being able to help the class  her only direct lines in this volume are in the prologue monologue  later appearances  with kaneda on the ship  are silent  recorded as a passing mention","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html#sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p12-1\">Depth review: the unspoken confession<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.12–13, 233–251<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Seaside monologue before the exam: Hiyori looks out at the ocean, alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;I am sorry, Ryuuen-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;Please forgive me for being so pathetic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Speaks in apologetic, self-effacing terms toward both Ryūen and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps her feelings to herself — admits she never said &quot;I like you&quot; because they are now enemies.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Resolves to defeat Ayanokōji so Class D can reach Class A; sees the exam as &quot;a path to survival and a path to death at the same time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Vows to inflict defeat on him while her feelings remain unchanged.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Apologises to him for not being able to help the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her only direct lines in this volume are in the prologue monologue; later appearances (with Kaneda on the ship) are silent, recorded as a passing mention.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p171-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Shiina&#x27;s resolve<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka depth review  survival game mastermind leads class c onto the uninhabited island for the third straight year  under the survival game exam rules   i surrender   there s nothing in the rules against it   i ll make it official here  runs out of ammunition against ryuuen and ibuki  eliminates ibuki with a paintball to the thigh  then defeats ryuuen by throwing a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on impact  allowed class b s surprise attack on his own class so that cornered class c would be forced to accept an alliance with ichinose s class d   then declares that alliance after class a is eliminated  identified class a s three vips by attacking at night and watching the guards rush to protect wang mei yu  sato maya and yukimura teruhiko  passed the names to class b  class c places second  the alliance with class d is now open  is the object of hiyori s unspoken confession  she resolves to defeat him in this exam  fights him on the beach  ryuuen concedes and vows no mercy from here on  declares the c d alliance with her class  commands him in class c  hashimoto loses a duel to hirata  uses her as recon commander over the radio","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-1\">Depth review: survival game mastermind<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.14–251<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leads Class C onto the uninhabited island for the third straight year, under the Survival Game exam rules.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I surrender.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;There&#x27;s nothing in the rules against it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ll make it official here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Runs out of ammunition against Ryuuen and Ibuki, eliminates Ibuki with a paintball to the thigh, then defeats Ryuuen by throwing a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on impact.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Allowed Class B&#x27;s surprise attack on his own class so that cornered Class C would be forced to accept an alliance with Ichinose&#x27;s Class D — then declares that alliance after Class A is eliminated.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Identified Class A&#x27;s three VIPs by attacking at night and watching the guards rush to protect Wang Mei-Yu, Satō Maya and Yukimura Teruhiko; passed the names to Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C places second; the alliance with Class D is now open.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Is the object of Hiyori&#x27;s unspoken confession; she resolves to defeat him in this exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Fights him on the beach; Ryuuen concedes and vows no mercy from here on.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Declares the C–D alliance with her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Commands him in Class C; Hashimoto loses a duel to Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Uses her as recon commander over the radio.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: the survival game opens<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi sanada-kousei shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 ch 1   depth read  the survival game opens arrives on the same uninhabited island for his third straight year  notes the grid is now a o   1 15  larger than last year s a j   1 10   maybe  but speculating now won t tell us anything   looks like we re finally arriving   an expulsion from the class whose three vip s get taken out first  huh  well  i figured they d pull something like that  concludes the expulsion can be minimized  victims with protection points  but that fear of expulsion will force combat eventually   a draw decided by luck is worse  class c starts at area e12  ryuen c12  horikita g12  ichinose i12  talks through the rules and strategy with him on the ship and beach  has him draw the starting position lot  hears her point about the food shortage forcing event participation  exam rules  3 nights 4 days  roles commander vip guard analyst scout  global gps shutdown  1  individual  3  identity check  5  first wiped out class selects one for expulsion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: the survival game opens<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives on the same uninhabited island for his third straight year; notes the grid is now A–O × 1–15 (larger than last year&#x27;s A–J × 1–10).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sanada-kousei.html\">Sanada Kōsei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Maybe. But speculating now won&#x27;t tell us anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Looks like we&#x27;re finally arriving.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;An expulsion from the class whose three VIP&#x27;s get taken out first, huh? Well, I figured they&#x27;d pull something like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Concludes the expulsion can be minimized (victims with Protection Points) but that fear of expulsion will force combat eventually — a draw decided by luck is worse.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C starts at area E12 (Ryūen C12, Horikita G12, Ichinose I12).<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Talks through the rules and strategy with him on the ship and beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sanada Kōsei<\/b> Has him draw the starting-position lot.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Hears her point about the food shortage forcing event participation.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Exam rules: 3 nights/4 days; roles Commander/VIP/Guard/Analyst/Scout; Global GPS Shutdown ×1, Individual ×3, Identity Check ×5; first wiped-out class selects one for expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-1\">← Before: Depth review: survival game mastermind<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p49-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: the ambush and the alliance reveal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p15-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi year 3  vol  3 ch 1   depth read  hashimoto s read on the exam  ah  i m sleepy  i should ve gone to bed a little earlier yesterday   but isn t this unbearable for students preparing for entrance exams  being pulled away from their desks at this time of year   an expulsion from the class whose three vip s get taken out first  huh  well  i figured they d pull something like that   for now  we keep our distance from the other classes and wait things out  yeah  let s just have them crush each other  sleepy and complaining about the timing  but reads the exam s expulsion mechanic quickly  favors a passive strategy of letting other classes fight  chats through the rules and strategy with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p15-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s read on the exam<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Ah~, I&#x27;m sleepy. I should&#x27;ve gone to bed a little earlier yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;But isn&#x27;t this unbearable for students preparing for entrance exams? Being pulled away from their desks at this time of year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;An expulsion from the class whose three VIP&#x27;s get taken out first, huh? Well, I figured they&#x27;d pull something like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For now, we keep our distance from the other classes and wait things out, yeah? Let&#x27;s just have them crush each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sleepy and complaining about the timing, but reads the exam&#x27;s expulsion mechanic quickly; favors a passive strategy of letting other classes fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Chats through the rules and strategy with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p47-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s reactions to the ambush<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shimazaki-ikkei-y3v3-p31-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"sugio-hiroshi shimazaki-ikkei","q":"shimazaki ikkei year 3  vol  3 ch 1   depth read  opposing the mountain plan  i m against it  other classes might be thinking something similar  besides  even if we force ourselves to cross the mountain  there s no guarantee that events will necessarily occur in the northeast  is there  cautious and analytical   rejects sugio s plan as risky and uncertain  opposes his mountain crossing proposal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shimazaki-ikkei-y3v3-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html#sc-shimazaki-ikkei-y3v3-p31-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: opposing the mountain plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sugio-hiroshi.html\">Sugio Hiroshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m against it. Other classes might be thinking something similar. Besides, even if we force ourselves to cross the mountain, there&#x27;s no guarantee that events will necessarily occur in the northeast, is there?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cautious and analytical — rejects Sugio&#x27;s plan as risky and uncertain.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sugio Hiroshi<\/b> Opposes his mountain-crossing proposal.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p31-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka shiraishi-asuka","q":"shiraishi asuka year 3  vol  3 ch 1   depth read  the food problem  looking at the rules  if we can keep running away  we won t lose for the time being  paintballs won t be consumed unless we fight  but the food problem is unavoidable  points out the meager food forces event participation and combat   a sharp strategic observation  shares her analysis of the food supply constraint","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html#sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p31-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: the food problem<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;Looking at the rules, if we can keep running away, we won&#x27;t lose for the time being. Paintballs won&#x27;t be consumed unless we fight, but the food problem is unavoidable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Points out the meager food forces event participation and combat — a sharp strategic observation.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Shares her analysis of the food/supply constraint.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p52-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Shiraishi as VIP and messenger<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sugio-hiroshi-y3v3-p31-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"shimazaki-ikkei sugio-hiroshi","q":"sugio hiroshi year 3  vol  3 ch 1   depth read  the mountain crossing proposal  i definitely think aiming for nearby events is dangerous  if we re going to shoulder the risk of fighting poorly and getting out  why don t we just avoid class a from the start and cross the mountain   not moving  huh  i don t intend to deny that  but if we do that  it means we re resolving ourselves to a shootout right from the start  doesn t it  proposes crossing the mountain to monopolize northeast events  argues against a passive strategy  his proposal is opposed by him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sugio-hiroshi-y3v3-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sugio-hiroshi.html#sc-sugio-hiroshi-y3v3-p31-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: the mountain-crossing proposal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sugio-hiroshi.html\">Sugio Hiroshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sugio Hiroshi<\/b> &quot;I definitely think aiming for nearby events is dangerous. If we&#x27;re going to shoulder the risk of fighting poorly and getting out, why don&#x27;t we just avoid Class A from the start and cross the mountain?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sugio Hiroshi<\/b> &quot;Not moving, huh? I don&#x27;t intend to deny that, but if we do that, it means we&#x27;re resolving ourselves to a shootout right from the start, doesn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Proposes crossing the mountain to monopolize northeast events; argues against a passive strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> His proposal is opposed by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p47-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi year 3  vol  3 ch 2   depth read  hashimoto s reactions to the ambush  let s hear it   if ryuuen and his crew are heading for b10  that means they ll come out by the sea   ayanokouji kiyotaka said as much  but when push comes to shove  hashimoto masayoshi is our only choice   a surprise attack  huh  that bastard ryuuen  he took on a pretty big risk  didn t he  manages communications and the map  jokes about being the expulsion sacrifice  and reacts with a mix of frustration and admiration to ryuen s gambit  relays his instructions  notes his lack of fighting spirit  admires the risky surprise attack","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p47-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s reactions to the ambush<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Let&#x27;s hear it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;If Ryuuen and his crew are heading for B10, that means they&#x27;ll come out by the sea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji Kiyotaka said as much, but when push comes to shove, Hashimoto Masayoshi is our only choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A surprise attack, huh... That bastard Ryuuen, he took on a pretty big risk, didn&#x27;t he?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Manages communications and the map, jokes about being the expulsion sacrifice, and reacts with a mix of frustration and admiration to Ryūen&#x27;s gambit.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Relays his instructions; notes his lack of fighting spirit.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Admires the risky surprise attack.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p15-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s read on the exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p101-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Hashimoto rallies the gloomy class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p49-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kitou-hayato hashimoto-masayoshi shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 ch 2   depth read  the ambush and the alliance reveal  even if we were to pick up the pace  the enemy would find out within five minutes  if they knew we d quickened our movement  class a would do the same   yeah  if i determine the supplies are necessary  i ll go for them without hesitation   i believe this class s ultimate goal  the rank we should be aiming for  is second place   the reason is simple and clear  i m thinking we can give first place to ichinose s class   you could say a provisional agreement has been made  the other side is keen on it   everyone  run  now   the answer is quite simple  ryuuen s class deliberately kept its distance after the start to make it seem like they were avoiding engagement  rotates a magazine removed weapon to each vip as misdirection so enemies cannot identify vips by their lack of a gun  deduced ryuen s fake retreat   global gps shutdown ambush from the frozen position updates  is asked by him to confirm he aims to win  relies on his counterattack during the ambush  relays instructions and reports  both react to the ambush  vip in the front row  struggles to keep up during the retreat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p49-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: the ambush and the alliance reveal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Even if we were to pick up the pace, the enemy would find out within five minutes. If they knew we&#x27;d quickened our movement, Class A would do the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Yeah. If I determine the supplies are necessary, I&#x27;ll go for them without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I believe this class&#x27;s ultimate goal, the rank we should be aiming for, is second place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The reason is simple and clear. I&#x27;m thinking we can give first place to Ichinose&#x27;s class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You could say a provisional agreement has been made. The other side is keen on it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Everyone, run! Now!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The answer is quite simple. Ryuuen&#x27;s class deliberately kept its distance after the start to make it seem like they were avoiding engagement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Rotates a magazine-removed weapon to each VIP as misdirection so enemies cannot identify VIPs by their lack of a gun.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Deduced Ryūen&#x27;s fake-retreat + Global GPS Shutdown ambush from the frozen position updates.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Is asked by him to confirm he aims to win; relies on his counterattack during the ambush.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Relays instructions and reports; both react to the ambush.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> VIP in the front row; struggles to keep up during the retreat.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: the survival game opens<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: pressure, provisioning and camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p52-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka shimazaki-ikkei shiraishi-asuka","q":"shiraishi asuka year 3  vol  3 ch 2   depth read  shiraishi as vip and messenger  h9  on his own does that mean it s koenji   i was able to confirm that the gps at h9 is koenji kun s  his role is apparently a guard  acts as a vip and radio messenger to the commander  confirms koenji split off  struggles to keep up during the retreat and can t communicate due to exhaustion  relays reports and is placed in the front row as a vip  receives intel from him as commander  via radio","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html#sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p52-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Shiraishi as VIP and messenger<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;H9? On his own?...Does that mean it&#x27;s Koenji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;I was able to confirm that the GPS at H9 is Koenji-kun&#x27;s. His role is apparently a guard.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Acts as a VIP and radio messenger to the commander; confirms Koenji split off; struggles to keep up during the retreat and can&#x27;t communicate due to exhaustion.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Relays reports and is placed in the front row as a VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Receives intel from him as commander (via radio).<span class=\"pg\">p.46–74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p31-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.1 — depth read: the food problem<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p117-1\">→ After: Depth review: Class C&#x27;s recon commander<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morishita-ai-y3v3-p56-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai","q":"morishita ai year 3  vol  3 ch 2   depth read  morishita s complaints and exhaustion  i m not pleased with being placed in the middle row  ayanokouji kiyotaka  i m the main strength of this class   to demote me and place a traitor in the front row instead  it seems we ve been saddled with an incompetent leader   this special exam is on a deserted island  so the rewards are pretty huge  y know   hah  hah  i suppose this is because i ran a full marathon in the schoolyard yesterday  isn t it  hah  complains about her placement and calls others names  traitor   tissue paper  but lags furthest behind on the retreat   an  amazoness of the dense forest  who overexerts herself  complain about her middle row placement  calls him a traitor and argues with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morishita-ai-y3v3-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html#sc-morishita-ai-y3v3-p56-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Morishita&#x27;s complaints and exhaustion<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m not pleased with being placed in the middle row, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka. I&#x27;m the main strength of this class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;To demote me and place a traitor in the front row instead... It seems we&#x27;ve been saddled with an incompetent leader.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> &quot;This special exam is on a deserted island, so the rewards are pretty huge, y&#x27;know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hah... hah... I suppose this is because I ran a full marathon in the schoolyard yesterday, isn&#x27;t it... hah.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Complains about her placement and calls others names (traitor, &quot;tissue paper&quot;), but lags furthest behind on the retreat — an &quot;Amazoness of the Dense Forest&quot; who overexerts herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Complain about her middle-row placement.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Calls him a traitor and argues with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kitou-hayato-y3v3-p63-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kitou-hayato","q":"kito hayato year 3  vol  3 ch 2   depth read  kitou s counterattack  let me confirm something  just to be sure  you re aiming to take first place in this exam  am i right to think that   a survival game  this feels like nothing more than playtime  but if we re aiming to win  i m going to take this seriously   in other words  you re not confident  during the surprise attack  takes cover behind a tree and counterattacks  taking out an enemy and halting the assault   showing skill despite never having fired in a real fight  intense and serious about winning  his intuition senses ayanokoji s lack of fighting spirit  and he acts decisively in the ambush  presses him for a commitment to win  backs up the retreat with his counterattack","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kitou-hayato-y3v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kitou-hayato.html#sc-kitou-hayato-y3v3-p63-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Kitou&#x27;s counterattack<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> &quot;Let me confirm something, just to be sure. You&#x27;re aiming to take first place in this exam... Am I right to think that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> &quot;A survival game... This feels like nothing more than playtime, but if we&#x27;re aiming to win, I&#x27;m going to take this seriously.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> &quot;...In other words, you&#x27;re not confident?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> During the surprise attack, takes cover behind a tree and counterattacks, taking out an enemy and halting the assault — showing skill despite never having fired in a real fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Intense and serious about winning; his intuition senses Ayanokōji&#x27;s lack of fighting spirit, and he acts decisively in the ambush.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Presses him for a commitment to win; backs up the retreat with his counterattack.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yoshida-kenta-y3v3-p72-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yoshida-kenta","q":"yoshida kenta year 3  vol  3 ch 2   depth read  yoshida s panic and questions  what the hell   so they used their one time only big move right from the get go   thinking about it normally  there was no way to defend against that surprise attack  was there  it s a flaw in the rules  urges learning to handle weapons before fighting  panics and grumbles at the surprise attack  calling it a rules flaw  argues for stopping to let class a pass and learn the guns","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yoshida-kenta-y3v3-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yoshida-kenta.html#sc-yoshida-kenta-y3v3-p72-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Yoshida&#x27;s panic and questions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> &quot;What the hell!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> &quot;So they used their one-time-only big move right from the get-go...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> &quot;Thinking about it normally, there was no way to defend against that surprise attack, was there...? It&#x27;s a flaw in the rules.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Urges learning to handle weapons before fighting; panics and grumbles at the surprise attack, calling it a rules flaw.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Argues for stopping to let Class A pass and learn the guns.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p86-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru year 3  vol  3 ch 3   depth read  ryuen s caution after the ambush looks down at the shattered class c students after the surprise attack   yeah  if things go well  that s eighteen people  not bad   it s probably better if kondou doesn t catch up   no send ten people   no  this is as far as we go   he held out longer than i expected   the problem is we failed to take down the one guy we needed to  sends a ten person search party  with vip yamashita  so identify person can t cheaply reveal the vip  calls off the pursuit because ayanokoji survived  decisive and ruthlessly rational   struck first to deny ayanokoji time to think  and values the psychological proof that ayanokoji has openings more than the casualties  launched the ambush to defeat him before he could plan  regrets failing to take him out  receives casualty reports and gives orders  holds him back from pursuing class c","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p86-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Ryūen&#x27;s caution after the ambush<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Looks down at the shattered Class C students after the surprise attack.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Yeah. If things go well, that&#x27;s eighteen people. Not bad.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s probably better if Kondou doesn&#x27;t catch up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;No—send ten people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, this is as far as we go.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He held out longer than I expected.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The problem is we failed to take down the one guy we needed to.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Sends a ten-person search party (with VIP Yamashita) so Identify Person can&#x27;t cheaply reveal the VIP; calls off the pursuit because Ayanokōji survived.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Decisive and ruthlessly rational — struck first to deny Ayanokōji time to think, and values the psychological proof that Ayanokōji has openings more than the casualties.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Launched the ambush to defeat him before he could plan; regrets failing to take him out.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Receives casualty reports and gives orders.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Holds him back from pursuing Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p89-1\">→ After: Depth review: the defeated rival<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p89-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru depth review  the defeated rival orders his class b to withdraw from the surprise attack on class c after kito holds out longer than expected   sounds like you were pretty successful   i just wanna know  is this really you surrendering   you  threw it   i ve seen your process of using any environment to win  calls off the ambush on class c when the reserve he expected to exploit does not materialise  katsuragi and ishizaki question the caution  obsessed with victory   chooses the 2 v 1 against ayanokoji over the safer shot at a vip because  settling things by running away on a rare occasion like this  is not fun  is beaten by a thrown paintball after burning his ammunition chasing ayanokoji onto the beach  concedes defeat and declares he will show no mercy in the truest sense from now on  fights him on the beach after ayanokoji fed class b the vip names  loses and vows revenge  fights alongside her  she is eliminated first and protests bitterly  discusses the withdrawal decision with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p89-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p89-1\">Depth review: the defeated rival<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.89–250<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Orders his Class B to withdraw from the surprise attack on Class C after Kitō holds out longer than expected.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Sounds like you were pretty successful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;I just wanna know, is this really you surrendering?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;You... threw it...!?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ve seen your process of using any environment to win.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Calls off the ambush on Class C when the reserve he expected to exploit does not materialise; Katsuragi and Ishizaki question the caution.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Obsessed with victory — chooses the 2-v-1 against Ayanokōji over the safer shot at a VIP because &quot;settling things by running away on a rare occasion like this&quot; is not fun.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Is beaten by a thrown paintball after burning his ammunition chasing Ayanokōji onto the beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Concedes defeat and declares he will show no mercy in the truest sense from now on.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Fights him on the beach after Ayanokōji fed Class B the VIP names; loses and vows revenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Fights alongside her; she is eliminated first and protests bitterly.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Discusses the withdrawal decision with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p86-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Ryūen&#x27;s caution after the ambush<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p120-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Ryūen deliberates the next attack<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"yamamura-miki hashimoto-masayoshi matoba-shinji ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 ch 3   depth read  pressure  provisioning and camp  if you  yamamura  can just stay in for even one second longer without getting out  that alone is useful   head north and class a s there to greet you  head east and it s class d  there s no escaping a scenario where we get pincered by class b coming up from behind   if i were ryuuen no  if i were any other class  i d be grateful to see class c moving in one big clump   this is my decision as the one temporarily in charge of class c   i ll go to i10 alone   basically  if we don t attack  we won t be attacked  operate under that assumption   i can t say something baseless   i suppose it s because i don t dislike the deserted island exam itself  goes alone to i10 and secures food supplies while the d12 group draws class b away  divides provisions equally and explains small portion eating  rejects grouping up   it would let other classes ignore them and gather supplies freely   and splits the team to cover both food drops  reassures her that simply surviving is a contribution  discusses strategy and the gloomy mood  listens to his story in the tent  rebuts his group up and escape plans  reasons about how ryuen would exploit class c s mistakes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: pressure, provisioning and camp<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/matoba-shinji.html\">Matoba Shinji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If you, Yamamura, can just stay in for even one second longer without getting out, that alone is useful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Head north and Class A&#x27;s there to greet you; head east and it&#x27;s Class D. There&#x27;s no escaping a scenario where we get pincered by Class B coming up from behind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If I were Ryuuen—no, if I were any other class, I&#x27;d be grateful to see Class C moving in one big clump.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is my decision as the one temporarily in charge of Class C.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll go to I10 alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Basically, if we don&#x27;t attack, we won&#x27;t be attacked. Operate under that assumption.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t say something baseless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I suppose it&#x27;s because I don&#x27;t dislike the deserted island exam itself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Goes alone to I10 and secures food supplies while the D12 group draws Class B away; divides provisions equally and explains small-portion eating.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Rejects grouping up — it would let other classes ignore them and gather supplies freely — and splits the team to cover both food drops.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Reassures her that simply surviving is a contribution.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Discusses strategy and the gloomy mood; listens to his story in the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matoba Shinji<\/b> Rebuts his group-up and escape plans.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reasons about how Ryūen would exploit Class C&#x27;s mistakes.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p49-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: the ambush and the alliance reveal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p124-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji and the G11 offensive<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p94-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamamura-miki","q":"yamamura miki year 3  vol  3 ch 3   depth read  yamamura s fear and reassurance  it s just  it s scary  isn t it  if i get separated  i won t have any idea where my allies are or where the enemy is  right  anxious about being separated and feeling useless after class c lost nishikawa  a vip  nods with resolve after ayanokoji s reassurance  is reassured by him that simply surviving is a contribution","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamamura-miki.html#sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p94-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Yamamura&#x27;s fear and reassurance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s just... it&#x27;s scary, isn&#x27;t it? If I get separated, I won&#x27;t have any idea where my allies are or where the enemy is, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Anxious about being separated and feeling useless after Class C lost Nishikawa (a VIP); nods with resolve after Ayanokōji&#x27;s reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is reassured by him that simply surviving is a contribution.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p233-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the unseen final guard<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p96-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune year 3  vol  3 ch 3   depth read  horikita s disbelief and invisible pressure  my honest impression is   really  is it possible   ayanokouji kun is how should i put it  he s not the type of person to be careless in this kind of fight   i probably  just don t want to frankly acknowledge it  acknowledge ryuuen kun  who managed to get the better of him   but let s gratefully accept the result  the situation is now slightly in our favor   even without koenji kun  our situation isn t bad   still  i wonder why i can t feel relieved in the slightest  even though class c is in a jam  refuses to accept that ayanokoji could be defeated so easily   a dangerous  faith  that he has no weaknesses   yet moves north to gain distance  is unsettled by the  invisible pressure  he still exerts even half destroyed  discusses the exam with him  comforts her and vows to crush any class in a straight fight  expects him to retire at any moment  notes the large sum spent on his cooperation previously","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p96-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p96-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Horikita&#x27;s disbelief and invisible pressure<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;My honest impression is, &#x27;Really? Is it possible?&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun is—how should I put it... He&#x27;s not the type of person to be careless in this kind of fight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I probably... just don&#x27;t want to frankly acknowledge it. Acknowledge Ryuuen-kun, who managed to get the better of him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But let&#x27;s gratefully accept the result. The situation is now slightly in our favor.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even without Koenji-kun, our situation isn&#x27;t bad.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Still, I wonder why I can&#x27;t feel relieved in the slightest, even though Class C is in a jam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Refuses to accept that Ayanokōji could be defeated so easily — a dangerous &quot;faith&quot; that he has no weaknesses — yet moves north to gain distance.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is unsettled by the &quot;invisible pressure&quot; he still exerts even half-destroyed.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Discusses the exam with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Comforts her and vows to crush any class in a straight fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Expects him to retire at any moment; notes the large sum spent on his cooperation previously.<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p197-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Horikita on the final day<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p101-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi year 3  vol  3 ch 3   depth read  hashimoto rallies the gloomy class  ayanokouji kiyotaka  you could just charge in by yourself and annihilate the enemy unit  you know   man  everyone s lookin  so gloomy  well  can t be helped  given our results so far   isn t there somethin  you can say as our leader   anyway  i guess when things are this gloomy is when it s my time to shine  huh  keeps the class s morale up after the disastrous start  cheerful  a natural straight man  and tells a funny middle school bike story in the tent  admires his securing the i10 supplies alone and prods him to encourage the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p101-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Hashimoto rallies the gloomy class<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji Kiyotaka. You could just charge in by yourself and annihilate the enemy unit, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Man, everyone&#x27;s lookin&#x27; so gloomy. Well, can&#x27;t be helped, given our results so far.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Isn&#x27;t there somethin&#x27; you can say as our leader?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Anyway, I guess when things are this gloomy is when it&#x27;s my time to shine, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps the class&#x27;s morale up after the disastrous start; cheerful, a natural straight man, and tells a funny middle-school bike story in the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Admires his securing the I10 supplies alone and prods him to encourage the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p47-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s reactions to the ambush<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p151-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s lingering doubt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p117-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka shiraishi-asuka","q":"shiraishi asuka depth review  class c s recon commander speaks privately with ayanokoji after the surprise attack  assuring him she trusts him completely   at the very least  i trust you   then i ll make use of that trust without reservation   just as you said  ayanokouji kun  it s turned into quite a chaotic battle  hasn t it  acts as class c s commander over the radio  relaying other classes  positions and directing the gps jammer tactics  shows respect and a willingness to tell a  gentle lie  for someone s own good  or speak plainly when it is not   ayanokoji notes this diverges from his first impression of her  expresses no doubt about ayanokoji s leadership even after the failed prediction  which unsettles him  places unconditional trust in him and serves as his reconnaissance lead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html#sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p117-1\">Depth review: Class C&#x27;s recon commander<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.117–232<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Speaks privately with Ayanokōji after the surprise attack, assuring him she trusts him completely.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;At the very least, I trust you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;Then I&#x27;ll make use of that trust without reservation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;Just as you said, Ayanokouji-kun, it&#x27;s turned into quite a chaotic battle, hasn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Acts as Class C&#x27;s commander over the radio, relaying other classes&#x27; positions and directing the GPS-jammer tactics.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Shows respect and a willingness to tell a &quot;gentle lie&quot; for someone&#x27;s own good, or speak plainly when it is not — Ayanokōji notes this diverges from his first impression of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Expresses no doubt about Ayanokōji&#x27;s leadership even after the failed prediction, which unsettles him.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Places unconditional trust in him and serves as his reconnaissance lead.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p52-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.2 — depth read: Shiraishi as VIP and messenger<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p160-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Class D&#x27;s trust impresses<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p120-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru year 3  vol  3 ch 4   depth read  ryuen deliberates the next attack  i ve got him cornered  but how re you gonna move  ayanokouji   there s always the option of crushin  that eyesore class a first  but that d just make the guys at the bottom happy   the main target s always class c   it s the fear of not being able to see your opponent s face  the stronger the enemy  the more one s imagination is stirred up  obsessed with defeating ayanokoji but restrained by katsuragi  recognizes that even after a successful ambush  ayanokoji shows no sign of weakness  debates strategy with him  accepts the advice to stay defensive for now  focuses on him as the main target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p120-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Ryūen deliberates the next attack<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve got him cornered... but how&#x27;re you gonna move, Ayanokouji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;There&#x27;s always the option of crushin&#x27; that eyesore Class A first... but that&#x27;d just make the guys at the bottom happy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;The main target&#x27;s always Class C.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s the fear of not being able to see your opponent&#x27;s face. The stronger the enemy, the more one&#x27;s imagination is stirred up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Obsessed with defeating Ayanokōji but restrained by Katsuragi; recognizes that even after a successful ambush, Ayanokōji shows no sign of weakness.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Debates strategy with him; accepts the advice to stay defensive for now.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Focuses on him as the main target.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p89-1\">← Before: Depth review: the defeated rival<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-1\">→ After: Depth review: beach conversation with Hiyori<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p124-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ryuuen-kakeru hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 ch 4   depth read  koenji and the g11 offensive  that s our common understanding  but there s just a certain  creepiness to it  it s because i don t understand the reason why he s still here instead of retiring   right now  everyone s focused on moving around the island  gathering supplies and staying healthy  but that s nothing more than a prelude   we re leaving now  we re going to secure the supplies and food at g11   enough idle talk  it s precisely because the enemy is closer that we must get there first   we ll wait here for five minutes   we re not using any tactics  if we save them  the enemy will have to remain constantly on guard  chooses to go on the offensive for g11 and deliberately delays twice by five minutes  saving tactics and exploiting the enemy s need to stay vigilant    i already knew the result  deduces the exam s true endgame is a chaotic firefight in a shrinking area  where stray rounds could eliminate vips  puzzled that he hasn t retired  keeps monitoring him as a wild card  anticipates his moves at g11 and positions the class for the confrontation  relies on him to steady the anxious class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p124-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji and the G11 offensive<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s our common understanding, but there&#x27;s just a certain... creepiness to it. It&#x27;s because I don&#x27;t understand the reason why he&#x27;s still here instead of retiring.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Right now, everyone&#x27;s focused on moving around the island, gathering supplies and staying healthy, but that&#x27;s nothing more than a prelude.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;We&#x27;re leaving now. We&#x27;re going to secure the supplies and food at G11.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Enough idle talk. It&#x27;s precisely because the enemy is closer that we must get there first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;ll wait here for five minutes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;re not using any tactics. If we save them, the enemy will have to remain constantly on guard.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Chooses to go on the offensive for G11 and deliberately delays twice by five minutes, saving tactics and exploiting the enemy&#x27;s need to stay vigilant — &quot;I already knew the result.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Deduces the exam&#x27;s true endgame is a chaotic firefight in a shrinking area, where stray rounds could eliminate VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Puzzled that he hasn&#x27;t retired; keeps monitoring him as a wild card.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Anticipates his moves at G11 and positions the class for the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Relies on him to steady the anxious class.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: pressure, provisioning and camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p152-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: sealing the alliance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p126-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami andou kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji year 3  vol  3 ch 4   depth read  kanzaki sees the shrinking map stares at the analyst s tablet as the 11 00 event s outer squares are marked as soon to be restricted   it s too early to draw conclusions  but if the next event has a similar mechanic  the probability will be orders of magnitude higher   there s no way to avoid a fight from here on   for now  we ll move to secure it  o14 has little land  so the supplies themselves should be easy to find   we ll split into three groups at once and head to collect the event rewards  sharp and analytical   immediately grasps that the map is shrinking and combat is now unavoidable  momentarily shaken  then refocused by ichinose s message  receives her message not to worry and not to push for o14  class d s analyst operates the tablet he reads","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p126-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Kanzaki sees the shrinking map<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stares at the analyst&#x27;s tablet as the 11:00 event&#x27;s outer squares are marked as soon-to-be restricted.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s too early to draw conclusions, but if the next event has a similar mechanic, the probability will be orders of magnitude higher.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;There&#x27;s no way to avoid a fight from here on—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;For now, we&#x27;ll move to secure it. O14 has little land, so the supplies themselves should be easy to find.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;ll split into three groups at once and head to collect the event rewards.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sharp and analytical — immediately grasps that the map is shrinking and combat is now unavoidable; momentarily shaken, then refocused by Ichinose&#x27;s message.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Receives her message not to worry and not to push for O14.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">andou<\/b> Class D&#x27;s analyst operates the tablet he reads.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p155-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Kanzaki&#x27;s armed scrutiny<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p131-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru morofuji-rika ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio depth review  the wild card eliminated ambushes a class b supply group surrounding morofuji  unseen  eliminating eight guards in under thirty seconds   die  ayanokouji   agh  dammit  so this is how it ends  single handedly picks off eight class b guards with precise submachine gun fire from cover  cocky and theatrical   thanks her victims for the fun  calls the encounter  an act of kindness  in koenji s own way  fiercely competitive  loud and profane when she loses  is hit by ayanokoji s final shot to the right thigh after her own spray runs dry  eliminated  complains she never wanted to take part in the exam  fights him alongside ryuen at the end  partners with him in the final 2 v 1  spares her and lets class b keep the supplies","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p131-1\">Depth review: the wild card eliminated<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.131–240<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ambushes a Class B supply group surrounding Morofuji, unseen, eliminating eight guards in under thirty seconds.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/morofuji-rika.html\">Morofuji Rika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Die, Ayanokouji!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Agh, dammit! So this is how it ends!?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Single-handedly picks off eight Class B guards with precise submachine-gun fire from cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Cocky and theatrical — thanks her victims for the fun, calls the encounter &quot;an act of kindness, in Koenji&#x27;s own way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fiercely competitive, loud and profane when she loses.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Is hit by Ayanokōji&#x27;s final shot to the right thigh after her own spray runs dry.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Eliminated; complains she never wanted to take part in the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Fights him alongside Ryūen at the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Partners with him in the final 2-v-1.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Spares her and lets Class B keep the supplies.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p236-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the wild card falls<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"morofuji-rika kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke depth review  the unreachable lone wolf appears unseen and eliminates eight class b guards around morofuji in under thirty seconds   you re the vip  aren t you   there is nothing to it  is there  i am from class a  you are from class b  we re enemies   for me  winning or losing this special exam is a matter of supreme indifference  single handedly dismantles a class b guard unit with precise  unseen fire  spares vip morofuji and lets her keep the supplies  courtly  theatrical and self assured    my  my  and grand pronouncements about the  great wilderness  acts purely for his own amusement  true to his word that winning or losing is a matter of indifference to him  spares her with a warning dressed as kindness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-1\">Depth review: the unreachable lone wolf<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.131–134<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears unseen and eliminates eight Class B guards around Morofuji in under thirty seconds.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/morofuji-rika.html\">Morofuji Rika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re the VIP, aren&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;There is nothing to it, is there? I am from Class A, you are from Class B. We&#x27;re enemies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;For me, winning or losing this special exam is a matter of supreme indifference.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Single-handedly dismantles a Class B guard unit with precise, unseen fire; spares VIP Morofuji and lets her keep the supplies.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Courtly, theatrical and self-assured — &quot;My, my...&quot; and grand pronouncements about the &quot;great wilderness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Acts purely for his own amusement; true to his word that winning or losing is a matter of indifference to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Spares her with a warning dressed as kindness.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-2\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji&#x27;s casual massacre<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"morofuji-rika komiya-kyogo kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke year 3  vol  3 ch 4   depth read  koenji s casual massacre ambushes class b s e9 supply group from the forest with unseen  precise shots   you re the vip  aren t you  if you were to fight back  you would simply be eliminated for nothing   there is nothing to it  is there  i am from class a  you are from class b  we re enemies   i enjoyed the uninhabited island for a day and thinking i had my fill  was on my way back to the ship but i thought i d give this a try for the novelty of it   for me  winning or losing this special exam is a matter of supreme indifference   very well  i shall take my leave now  i trust you will take care not to get in my way again  eliminates six of class b s eight guards in under thirty seconds without being seen  then spares vip morofuji and lets her keep the supplies  detached and theatrical   fights purely for amusement  indifferent to winning  yet his  kindness   sparing morofuji  doubles as a stern warning  spares her and lets her take the supplies  is baited by his shouting  which reveals their position  takes him out first","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-2\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji&#x27;s casual massacre<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ambushes Class B&#x27;s E9 supply group from the forest with unseen, precise shots.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/morofuji-rika.html\">Morofuji Rika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re the VIP, aren&#x27;t you? If you were to fight back, you would simply be eliminated for nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;There is nothing to it, is there? I am from Class A, you are from Class B. We&#x27;re enemies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;I enjoyed the uninhabited island for a day and thinking I had my fill, was on my way back to the ship—but I thought I&#x27;d give this a try for the novelty of it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For me, winning or losing this special exam is a matter of supreme indifference.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Very well. I shall take my leave now. I trust you will take care not to get in my way again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Eliminates six of Class B&#x27;s eight guards in under thirty seconds without being seen, then spares VIP Morofuji and lets her keep the supplies.<span class=\"pg\">p.130–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Detached and theatrical — fights purely for amusement, indifferent to winning, yet his &quot;kindness&quot; (sparing Morofuji) doubles as a stern warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Spares her and lets her take the supplies.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> Is baited by his shouting, which reveals their position; takes him out first.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y3v3-p131-1\">← Before: Depth review: the unreachable lone wolf<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p151-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi year 3  vol  3 ch 5   depth read  hashimoto s lingering doubt  we re lucky ayanokouji brought up the idea of an alliance   you re sure this is gonna be okay  right   i m going too and don t try to stop me  alright  if they start shootin  without askin  questions  i can be your shield  publicly champions the alliance to steady the class but privately doubts it  offers to shield ayanokoji  showing genuine loyalty  persuades classmates  voices doubts  and offers to protect him in negotiations","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p151-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s lingering doubt<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;We&#x27;re lucky Ayanokouji brought up the idea of an alliance.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re sure this is gonna be okay, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m going too and don&#x27;t try to stop me, alright? If they start shootin&#x27; without askin&#x27; questions, I can be your shield.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Publicly champions the alliance to steady the class but privately doubts it; offers to shield Ayanokōji, showing genuine loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Persuades classmates, voices doubts, and offers to protect him in negotiations.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p101-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Hashimoto rallies the gloomy class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p174-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Hashimoto on the shrinking area<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p152-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi kanzaki-ryuuji shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 ch 5   depth read  sealing the alliance  if you ve seen the kind of student ichinose is  you should understand that she can be trusted   it s not like taking first place one time will get them to class a   what s wrong  are you worried about the alliance after all   i suppose i ll gratefully accept your sentiment    to hashimoto offering to be his shield  let s join forces  that way  class c and class d can form a group of fifty   you should try to better understand just how incredible it is to be trusted  goes unarmed with hashimoto to negotiate the alliance with kanzaki s class d  securing their acceptance  trusts her to honor the alliance  she had pre briefed class d to accept them  persuades the class  hashimoto offers to shield him and voices private doubts  negotiates with him  defuses his armed welcome  and later urges him to trust in class d and know ichinose  discusses class d s trust with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p152-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: sealing the alliance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If you&#x27;ve seen the kind of student Ichinose is, you should understand that she can be trusted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s not like taking first place one time will get them to Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;What&#x27;s wrong? Are you worried about the alliance after all?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I suppose I&#x27;ll gratefully accept your sentiment.&quot; — to Hashimoto offering to be his shield<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s join forces. That way, Class C and Class D can form a group of fifty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should try to better understand just how incredible it is to be trusted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Goes unarmed with Hashimoto to negotiate the alliance with Kanzaki&#x27;s Class D, securing their acceptance.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Trusts her to honor the alliance; she had pre-briefed Class D to accept them.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Persuades the class; Hashimoto offers to shield him and voices private doubts.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Negotiates with him, defuses his armed welcome, and later urges him to trust in Class D and know Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Discusses Class D&#x27;s trust with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p124-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji and the G11 offensive<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: the solo plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p155-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami ayanokouji-atsuomi kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji year 3  vol  3 ch 5   depth read  kanzaki s armed scrutiny leads ten class d guards in a wall  guns trained on ayanokoji and hashimoto as they approach unarmed   i wonder about that  there s a possibility your allies are hiding nearby   just three people ain t gonna do nothin   if we defeat the two of you here  we can significantly lower our chances of coming in last  this is a golden opportunity   what if we trust you and are betrayed  that would be a crisis for our class   i forgot to tell you something important  regarding the chain of command from here on  ichinose has said to entrust everything to you  ayanokouji   you have the power to turn the tide of battle all by yourself  stern  loyal to ichinose and initially hostile  but principled   lowers his guns once briefed  yet remains troubled by why ayanokoji proposed the alliance  confronts him at gunpoint  then accepts the alliance and questions his motives  fully loyal  reports that she entrusted command to ayanokoji  admires ayanokoji s father  which colors his high opinion of ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p155-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Kanzaki&#x27;s armed scrutiny<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leads ten Class D guards in a wall, guns trained on Ayanokōji and Hashimoto as they approach unarmed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;I wonder about that. There&#x27;s a possibility your allies are hiding nearby.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;Just three people ain&#x27;t gonna do nothin&#x27;.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;If we defeat the two of you here, we can significantly lower our chances of coming in last. This is a golden opportunity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What if we trust you and are betrayed? That would be a crisis for our class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I forgot to tell you something important. Regarding the chain of command from here on, Ichinose has said to entrust everything to you, Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You have the power to turn the tide of battle all by yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Stern, loyal to Ichinose and initially hostile, but principled — lowers his guns once briefed, yet remains troubled by why Ayanokōji proposed the alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Confronts him at gunpoint, then accepts the alliance and questions his motives.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Fully loyal; reports that she entrusted command to Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> Admires Ayanokōji&#x27;s father, which colors his high opinion of Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p126-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Kanzaki sees the shrinking map<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p174-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Kanzaki&#x27;s report and debate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v3-p158-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kobashi-yume kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami year 3  vol  3 ch 5   depth read  ichinose s faith from afar watches the g11 battle on her tablet and  seeing class c flee  prepares her class to receive them   ayanokouji kun won t lose  no  i won t let him lose   if we absorb class c  we ll become the largest force   i need you to tell everyone in the class properly beforehand  ayanokouji kun will be making contact with class d  so when he does  make sure we absolutely do not attack first   i understand  ayanokouji kun  i know what you re thinking  calmly confident in ayanokoji despite his apparent blunders  orchestrates class d s reception of class c and pre empts any attack  trusts him completely  attributes his  carelessness  to a deeper plan  and entrusts command to him  vip  relays her instructions to the class  sends instructions via kobashi  kanzaki wonders whether the alliance benefits class d","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y3v3-p158-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y3v3-p158-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Ichinose&#x27;s faith from afar<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the G11 battle on her tablet and, seeing Class C flee, prepares her class to receive them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kobashi-yume.html\">Kobashi Yume<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun won&#x27;t lose. No, I won&#x27;t let him lose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;If we absorb Class C, we&#x27;ll become the largest force.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;I need you to tell everyone in the class properly beforehand. Ayanokouji-kun will be making contact with Class D, so when he does, make sure we absolutely do not attack first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand, Ayanokouji-kun. I know what you&#x27;re thinking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calmly confident in Ayanokōji despite his apparent blunders; orchestrates Class D&#x27;s reception of Class C and pre-empts any attack.<span class=\"pg\">p.158–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Trusts him completely, attributes his &quot;carelessness&quot; to a deeper plan, and entrusts command to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.158–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kobashi Yume<\/b> VIP; relays her instructions to the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.158–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Sends instructions via Kobashi; Kanzaki wonders whether the alliance benefits Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p160-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka shiraishi-asuka","q":"shiraishi asuka year 3  vol  3 ch 5   depth read  class d s trust impresses  the charm class d possesses is incredible  impressed by how warmly class d treats the wary class c members as equals  lowering their guard  discusses the alliance and class d s strength with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html#sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p160-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Class D&#x27;s trust impresses<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;The charm Class D possesses is incredible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Impressed by how warmly Class D treats the wary Class C members as equals, lowering their guard.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Discusses the alliance and Class D&#x27;s strength with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p117-1\">← Before: Depth review: Class C&#x27;s recon commander<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p230-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Shiraishi reports the chaos<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shibata-sou-y3v3-p162-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka shibata-sou","q":"shibata so year 3  vol  3 ch 5   depth read  shibata s interrupted greeting  h hey  ayanokouji  sorry to bother you before you eat  but you got a sec   uh  how should i put it  we re allies now  right  so  i just wanted to say hi  or something  nervous and eager to befriend ayanokoji now that they re allies  cut off by kanzaki before he can ask his question  tries to greet him at the campfire  flees when kanzaki intervenes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shibata-sou-y3v3-p162-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html#sc-shibata-sou-y3v3-p162-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Shibata&#x27;s interrupted greeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> &quot;H-Hey, Ayanokouji. Sorry to bother you before you eat, but you got a sec?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> &quot;Uh... how should I put it? We&#x27;re allies now, right? So, I just wanted to say hi, or something...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Nervous and eager to befriend Ayanokōji now that they&#x27;re allies; cut off by Kanzaki before he can ask his question.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Tries to greet him at the campfire; flees when Kanzaki intervenes.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p171-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru shiina-hiyori","q":"shiina hiyori year 3  vol  3 ch 6   depth read  shiina s resolve walking alone on the beach  smiling at the waves  when ryuen approaches   oh my  good morning  ryuuen kun   yes  we believe in your words  ryuuen kun and we will follow you  now and always   that s true  the structure of a story is such that readers are most moved when it turns from darkness to light   that it s best to be mentally prepared for whatever might happen   if it would be for the sake of everyone  for the sake of the class b that is so important to me   in that case i won t hesitate  no matter who my opponent is  or what the outcome may be  calm and perceptive   reads ryuen s state of mind  uses a novel metaphor to urge preparation for any outcome  and pledges unwavering loyalty even under a  cruel choice  reassures and advises him on the beach  declares she ll follow him no matter what","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html#sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p171-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Shiina&#x27;s resolve<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking alone on the beach, smiling at the waves, when Ryūen approaches.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;Oh my, good morning, Ryuuen-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;Yes. We believe in your words, Ryuuen-kun and we will follow you, now and always.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s true. The structure of a story is such that readers are most moved when it turns from darkness to light.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That it&#x27;s best to be mentally prepared for whatever might happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If it would be for the sake of everyone... for the sake of the Class B that is so important to me...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In that case—I won&#x27;t hesitate. No matter who my opponent is, or what the outcome may be.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and perceptive — reads Ryūen&#x27;s state of mind, uses a novel metaphor to urge preparation for any outcome, and pledges unwavering loyalty even under a &quot;cruel choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reassures and advises him on the beach; declares she&#x27;ll follow him no matter what.<span class=\"pg\">p.171–173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p12-1\">← Before: Depth review: the unspoken confession<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p172-1\">→ After: Depth review: beach conversation with Ryūen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru depth review  beach conversation with hiyori rolling up his map  approaches shiina on the beach and asks why she looks so pleased with herself   lookin  pretty happy all by yourself  shiina   there ain t nothin  to it   unfortunately  i m not a fan of stories with depressin  beginnings  declares he will win the exam  with my own damn power  forcefully masking his own indecisiveness  listens seriously to her novel ending metaphor about being prepared for any outcome  accepts her reaffirmation of class d s support","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-1\">Depth review: beach conversation with Hiyori<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.172–173<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Rolling up his map, approaches Shiina on the beach and asks why she looks so pleased with herself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Lookin&#x27; pretty happy all by yourself, Shiina.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;There ain&#x27;t nothin&#x27; to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Unfortunately, I&#x27;m not a fan of stories with depressin&#x27; beginnings.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Declares he will win the exam &quot;with my own damn power,&quot; forcefully masking his own indecisiveness.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Listens seriously to her novel-ending metaphor about being prepared for any outcome; accepts her reaffirmation of Class D&#x27;s support.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p120-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.4 — depth read: Ryūen deliberates the next attack<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-2\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Ryūen through Shiina<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei ibuki-mio ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru year 3  vol  3 ch 6   depth read  ryuen through shiina  lookin  pretty happy all by yourself  shiina   there ain t nothin  to it  i m gonna win this special exam and i m gonna do it with my own damn power   so in the end  it means we don t know shit about what s comin  huh   but still i ll force my way through with my own power  whatever it takes to take down ayanokouji   and that s even if i force some kinda cruel choice on you down the line  deliberates alone  feels forced onto the defensive by the alliance and refuses to react to ayanokoji s expectations   intent on winning his own way  speaks with her on the beach  tests her resolve with a malicious  cruel choice  question  vows to beat him  senses ayanokoji anticipated both attacking options  assesses the alliance and rejects allying with class a  discusses the situation with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-2\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Ryūen through Shiina<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Lookin&#x27; pretty happy all by yourself, Shiina.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;There ain&#x27;t nothin&#x27; to it. I&#x27;m gonna win this special exam and I&#x27;m gonna do it with my own damn power.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;So in the end, it means we don&#x27;t know shit about what&#x27;s comin&#x27;, huh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But still—I&#x27;ll force my way through with my own power. Whatever it takes to take down Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;And that&#x27;s even if I force some kinda cruel choice on you down the line?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberates alone, feels forced onto the defensive by the alliance and refuses to react to Ayanokōji&#x27;s expectations — intent on winning his own way.<span class=\"pg\">p.171–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Speaks with her on the beach; tests her resolve with a malicious &quot;cruel choice&quot; question.<span class=\"pg\">p.171–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Vows to beat him; senses Ayanokōji anticipated both attacking options.<span class=\"pg\">p.171–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Assesses the alliance and rejects allying with Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.167–170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Discusses the situation with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-1\">← Before: Depth review: beach conversation with Hiyori<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p236-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the duel lost, defeat conceded<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p172-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru shiina-hiyori","q":"shiina hiyori depth review  beach conversation with ryuen walks the beach and is approached by ryuen  who remarks on her being alone   since we re at the beach  i was taking a little walk   yes  we believe in your words  ryuuen kun and we will follow you  now and always   that it s best to be mentally prepared for whatever might happen   however  it s a wide world out there  there are many masterpieces that are sad from beginning to end  reads ryuen s state of mind from his expression and answers with a cheerful smile  reaffirms class d s faith in his leadership  uses a novel ending metaphor to warn him to be prepared for either victory or defeat  the page locator also hits the table of contents entry  prologue  shiina hiyori s monologue    not a content page  no scene entry required","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p172-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html#sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p172-1\">Depth review: beach conversation with Ryūen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.172–173<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks the beach and is approached by Ryūen, who remarks on her being alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;Since we&#x27;re at the beach, I was taking a little walk.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;Yes. We believe in your words, Ryuuen-kun and we will follow you, now and always.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;That it&#x27;s best to be mentally prepared for whatever might happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, it&#x27;s a wide world out there. There are many masterpieces that are sad from beginning to end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Ryūen&#x27;s state of mind from his expression and answers with a cheerful smile.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reaffirms Class D&#x27;s faith in his leadership; uses a novel-ending metaphor to warn him to be prepared for either victory or defeat.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page locator also hits the Table of Contents entry &quot;Prologue: Shiina Hiyori&#x27;s Monologue&quot; — not a content page, no scene entry required.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p171-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Shiina&#x27;s resolve<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p251-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: found in good spirits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kanzaki-ryuuji takemoto ninomiya-yui ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 ch 6   depth read  the solo plan  my bad  i had some business to take care of   the damage will only be greater if they lie to themselves and force it   there are broadly two methods for determining our plan  one is to envision the objective you wish to achieve and map out a path to it  the other is to gauge the enemy s aim and thwart their intentions   no  avoiding engagement is best for now  we ll stick to a defensive strategy   moving a little closer now would be the better option  h10 isn t a bad choice   class a is moving as planned  contact the commander now and tell them to disable my personal gps the moment the next gps update occurs   yeah  i m not coming back today  chooses a defensive strategy  letting the shrinking area force a general firefight   the development he s been waiting for  goes to retrieve g9 supplies then has his gps disabled  disappearing from the exam to execute a solo plan  i m not coming back today  reasons ryuen attacked class c specifically because ayanokoji is his arch rival  not class a  analyzes his motives and anticipates his final day move  explains his strategic reasoning to him  instructs him to disable his gps and handle the plan if he s  taken out  directs that she retire immediately due to fever","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: the solo plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ninomiya-yui.html\">Ninomiya Yui<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;My bad, I had some business to take care of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;The damage will only be greater if they lie to themselves and force it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;There are broadly two methods for determining our plan. One is to envision the objective you wish to achieve and map out a path to it. The other is to gauge the enemy&#x27;s aim and thwart their intentions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, avoiding engagement is best for now. We&#x27;ll stick to a defensive strategy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Moving a little closer now would be the better option. H10 isn&#x27;t a bad choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Class A is moving as planned. Contact the commander now and tell them to disable my personal GPS the moment the next GPS update occurs.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, I&#x27;m not coming back today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Chooses a defensive strategy, letting the shrinking area force a general firefight — the development he&#x27;s been waiting for.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Goes to retrieve G9 supplies then has his GPS disabled, disappearing from the exam to execute a solo plan (&quot;I&#x27;m not coming back today&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.183–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons Ryūen attacked Class C specifically because Ayanokōji is his arch-rival, not Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Analyzes his motives and anticipates his final-day move.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Explains his strategic reasoning to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">takemoto<\/b> Instructs him to disable his GPS and handle the plan if he&#x27;s &quot;taken out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ninomiya Yui<\/b> Directs that she retire immediately due to fever.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p152-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: sealing the alliance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p202-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: the mastermind&#x27;s final-day moves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p174-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi year 3  vol  3 ch 6   depth read  hashimoto on the shrinking area  but man  we re obviously runnin  low on supplies  we got nothin  but a bunch of starving folks over here  too   they re really testing us  but j5 and k10  that s just asking too much   we re inside the area and getting too close to the center is kinda sketchy   you re goin  too  ayanokouji  you can just save your strength for the final day  y know  worries about supplies and the shrinking area  and is concerned when ayanokoji decides to go on the supply run himself  discusses strategy and tries to talk him out of the supply run","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p174-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p174-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Hashimoto on the shrinking area<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;But man, we&#x27;re obviously runnin&#x27; low on supplies. We got nothin&#x27; but a bunch of starving folks over here, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;They&#x27;re really testing us... but J5 and K10? That&#x27;s just asking too much.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;We&#x27;re inside the area and getting too close to the center is kinda sketchy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re goin&#x27; too, Ayanokouji? You can just save your strength for the final day, y&#x27;know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Worries about supplies and the shrinking area, and is concerned when Ayanokōji decides to go on the supply run himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Discusses strategy and tries to talk him out of the supply run.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p151-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s lingering doubt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p221-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s duel with Hirata<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p174-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi moriyama kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji year 3  vol  3 ch 6   depth read  kanzaki s report and debate  i was just saying that we ve reached a difficult phase  we ve used most of our handheld provisions   also  sumida and minamikata have seemed somewhat unwell since this morning   that s right  i want to avoid the risk of pushing ourselves unnecessarily  losing stamina  or getting injured   to prevent them from narrowing down our vip  we ll assign several mobile guards from our class   however  waiting right on the edge of the designated area has its own risks  practical and cautious   reports the alliance s dwindling supplies and illness  and argues for positioning at h10 for flexibility  receives his strategic explanations and carries out supply positioning plans  debates positioning with him  sends him to relay ayanokoji s words to the unwell students","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p174-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p174-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Kanzaki&#x27;s report and debate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/moriyama.html\">Moriyama<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;I was just saying that we&#x27;ve reached a difficult phase. We&#x27;ve used most of our handheld provisions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;Also, Sumida and Minamikata have seemed somewhat unwell since this morning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s right. I want to avoid the risk of pushing ourselves unnecessarily, losing stamina, or getting injured.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;To prevent them from narrowing down our VIP, we&#x27;ll assign several mobile guards from our class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, waiting right on the edge of the designated area has its own risks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Practical and cautious — reports the alliance&#x27;s dwindling supplies and illness, and argues for positioning at H10 for flexibility.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Receives his strategic explanations and carries out supply/positioning plans.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Debates positioning with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Moriyama<\/b> Sends him to relay Ayanokōji&#x27;s words to the unwell students.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p155-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Kanzaki&#x27;s armed scrutiny<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p233-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the guard who relays the map<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ninomiya-yui-y3v3-p182-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"amikura-mako ayanokouji-kiyotaka ninomiya-yui","q":"ninomiya yui year 3  vol  3 ch 6   depth read  ninomiya s fever found lying in the shade of a tree  breathing heavily  having fallen ill with a fever   she hasn t been feeling well since this morning  i think she s started running a fever  too ill to pretend she s fine  coughing and in pain  she is ordered to retire and be picked up by the school  amikura stays anxiously by her side  he orders her immediate retirement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ninomiya-yui-y3v3-p182-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ninomiya-yui.html#sc-ninomiya-yui-y3v3-p182-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Ninomiya&#x27;s fever<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ninomiya-yui.html\">Ninomiya Yui<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Found lying in the shade of a tree, breathing heavily, having fallen ill with a fever.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/amikura-mako.html\">Amikura Mako<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amikura Mako<\/b> &quot;She hasn&#x27;t been feeling well since this morning... I think she&#x27;s started running a fever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Too ill to pretend she&#x27;s fine; coughing and in pain, she is ordered to retire and be picked up by the school.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amikura Mako<\/b> Amikura stays anxiously by her side.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He orders her immediate retirement.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p197-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken hirata-yousuke hondou-ryoutaro horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune year 3  vol  3 ch 7   depth read  horikita on the final day breaks down camp early  tense  the final day begins with four classes a stone s throw apart   fortunately  it was only the guards who were taken out   that s not a bad idea  in fact  that s probably the correct answer  i was thinking the same thing    on moving g8 e9  stop that  hondou kun  forcibly surrounding him here won t solve anything   we are to maintain a suitable distance and wait for 9 00 a m   don t  i m sure it s no use   if he had resolved to fight us at nine o clock sharp  we could defeat him  but i m sure he won t fight  bloodthirsty toward ayanokoji for the surprise attack yet restrained   keeps a legal path open  stops sudo chasing  and uses her gps protection point strategy defensively  deeply unsettled by his raid  predicts he ll flee and refuses to send sudo after him  consults with him  holds him back from chasing ayanokoji  plans the final positioning and tactic timing with him  stops him from illegally surrounding ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p197-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p197-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Horikita on the final day<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Breaks down camp early, tense; the final day begins with four classes a stone&#x27;s throw apart.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Fortunately, it was only the guards who were taken out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s not a bad idea... In fact, that&#x27;s probably the correct answer. I was thinking the same thing.&quot; — on moving G8→E9<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Stop that, Hondou-kun. Forcibly surrounding him here won&#x27;t solve anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We are to maintain a suitable distance and wait for 9:00 a.m.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t... I&#x27;m sure it&#x27;s no use.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If he had resolved to fight us at nine o&#x27;clock sharp, we could defeat him. But I&#x27;m sure he won&#x27;t fight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Bloodthirsty toward Ayanokōji for the surprise attack yet restrained — keeps a legal path open, stops Sudō chasing, and uses her GPS/Protection Point strategy defensively.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Deeply unsettled by his raid; predicts he&#x27;ll flee and refuses to send Sudō after him.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Consults with him; holds him back from chasing Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Plans the final positioning and tactic timing with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/b> Stops him from illegally surrounding Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y3v3-p96-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Horikita&#x27;s disbelief and invisible pressure<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y3v3-p198-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"satou-maya horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken year 3  vol  3 ch 7   depth read  sudo protects sato  what are we gonna do  suzune  about him   yesterday seriously had me in a cold sweat   isn t it because you re here  sudou kun   if that s what it takes to win  maybe that s what i should do  but i m not gonna let  em take you out this easily  we just gotta fight  pulls sato out of a paintball barrage and leaps out to draw the enemy fire aimed at her  bloodthirsty toward ayanokoji but fiercely protective of sato  willing to sacrifice himself to save her  saves her from being eliminated  recognizes she s the vip class b is targeting  discusses ayanokoji  is held back from chasing him  deeply resentful of his surprise attack on class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y3v3-p198-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y3v3-p198-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Sudō protects Satō<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;What are we gonna do, Suzune? About him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Yesterday seriously had me in a cold sweat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> &quot;Isn&#x27;t it because you&#x27;re here, Sudou-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If that&#x27;s what it takes to win, maybe that&#x27;s what I should do. But I&#x27;m not gonna let &#x27;em take you out this easily... We just gotta fight!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Pulls Satō out of a paintball barrage and leaps out to draw the enemy fire aimed at her.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Bloodthirsty toward Ayanokōji but fiercely protective of Satō; willing to sacrifice himself to save her.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Saves her from being eliminated; recognizes she&#x27;s the VIP Class B is targeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses Ayanokōji; is held back from chasing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Deeply resentful of his surprise attack on Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p202-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune shiraishi-asuka satou-maya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 ch 7   depth read  the mastermind s final day moves  the right call  headquarters is undoubtedly tracking every student s gps in real time  24 7   what am i planning  nothing  if there s a path  i ll walk it   we kept losing points in the beginning  i m glad i could make up for it  even just a little   there was something i came to understand from infiltrating class a  it was that class a was slightly lacking the tension it should ve had   appoint a commander  gather supplies  keep your distance  read the enemy s movements and avoid engagement   the objective wasn t to eliminate as many people as possible  but to find out who the vips were   if they could have predicted the attack beforehand  it could ve been a feint   now  all that s left is to take out the remaining class b students and this special exam will be over   adjustments  identified class a s three vips via the previous night s attack and passed the names to class b to catalyze an assault  aims to throw the battlefield into chaos so students panic and eliminate each other  then escape the vips  walks the path she leaves open  reads that she expects him to flee  has her report the battlefield state  leaves her with yamamura  identified her as a class a vip  her elimination narrows class a to one vip","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p202-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: the mastermind&#x27;s final-day moves<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;The right call. Headquarters is undoubtedly tracking every student&#x27;s GPS in real-time, 24/7.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;What am I planning? Nothing. If there&#x27;s a path, I&#x27;ll walk it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;We kept losing points in the beginning. I&#x27;m glad I could make up for it, even just a little.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There was something I came to understand from infiltrating Class A. It was that Class A was slightly lacking the tension it should&#x27;ve had.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Appoint a commander, gather supplies, keep your distance, read the enemy&#x27;s movements and avoid engagement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The objective wasn&#x27;t to eliminate as many people as possible, but to find out who the VIPs were.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If they could have predicted the attack beforehand, it could’ve been a feint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Now, all that&#x27;s left is to take out the remaining Class B students and this special exam will be over.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Adjustments.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Identified Class A&#x27;s three VIPs via the previous night&#x27;s attack and passed the names to Class B to catalyze an assault.<span class=\"pg\">p.231–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Aims to throw the battlefield into chaos so students panic and eliminate each other, then escape the VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Walks the path she leaves open; reads that she expects him to flee.<span class=\"pg\">p.201–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Has her report the battlefield state; leaves her with Yamamura.<span class=\"pg\">p.230–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Identified her as a Class A VIP; her elimination narrows Class A to one VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: the solo plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the bluff and the true goal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-satou-maya-y3v3-p217-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka satou-maya","q":"sato maya year 3  vol  3 ch 7   depth read  sato  targeted vip is almost showered in paintballs as class b concentrates fire on her  having learned she s a class a vip  terrified  hides in the tent during ayanokoji s previous night raid   the moment that likely exposed the vips  identities  is saved by him and urges him to flee and protect the other vips  suspects her vip identity was exposed when he raided the camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-satou-maya-y3v3-p217-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/satou-maya.html#sc-satou-maya-y3v3-p217-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Satō, targeted VIP<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is almost showered in paintballs as Class B concentrates fire on her, having learned she&#x27;s a Class A VIP.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Terrified, hides in the tent during Ayanokōji&#x27;s previous-night raid — the moment that likely exposed the VIPs&#x27; identities.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Is saved by him and urges him to flee and protect the other VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Suspects her VIP identity was exposed when he raided the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p221-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka matoba-shinji hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi year 3  vol  3 ch 7   depth read  hashimoto s duel with hirata is caught in the allied advance when class a splits its forces  faces hirata in a close range firefight   what s going on   take us out with a small group  are they serious   not bad  hirata  you re way more skilled than i thought  there s no hesitation or mercy in your aim   never seen you with such a desperate look on your face before  did getting abandoned by ayanokouji really piss you off that much   ayanokouji was sayin  he felt bad about what he did to you  hirata   that was some serious spirit  hirata  this match is my loss  duels hirata  uses taunts about ayanokoji to rattle him  but is eliminated by a slightly faster shot  praises hirata s spirit  duel opponent  is nearly shot again after being eliminated  uses his abandonment of hirata as psychological ammunition  matoba is shot beside him  he flees","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p221-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s duel with Hirata<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is caught in the allied advance when Class A splits its forces; faces Hirata in a close-range firefight.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/matoba-shinji.html\">Matoba Shinji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;What&#x27;s going on...?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Take us out with a small group? Are they serious?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Not bad, Hirata... You&#x27;re way more skilled than I thought. There&#x27;s no hesitation or mercy in your aim.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Never seen you with such a desperate look on your face before! Did getting abandoned by Ayanokouji really piss you off that much?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji was sayin&#x27; he felt bad about what he did to you, Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;...That was some serious spirit, Hirata. This match is my loss.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Duels Hirata, uses taunts about Ayanokōji to rattle him, but is eliminated by a slightly faster shot; praises Hirata&#x27;s spirit.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Duel opponent; is nearly shot again after being eliminated.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Uses his abandonment of Hirata as psychological ammunition.<span class=\"pg\">p.223–226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matoba Shinji<\/b> Matoba is shot beside him; he flees.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p174-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Hashimoto on the shrinking area<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p222-1\">→ After: Depth review: the duel lost<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p222-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi depth review  the duel lost faces hirata in the forest after class a s guard units are split up  outnumbered and without his vip nearby   not bad  hirata  you re way more skilled than i thought   never seen you with such a desperate look on your face before   that was some serious spirit  hirata   guess i pushed the honor student a little too far  fights a disciplined close range duel  uses psychological taunts about ayanokoji abandoning hirata  and is eliminated by a slightly faster shot to the chest  frank and observant  admits respect for an opponent mid fight  quick to read the killing intent in hirata s aim  loses narrowly to hirata  is left shaken when hirata raises the gun again after the match is decided  duel opponent  praises his spirit  then fears for his life when the trigger is squeezed partway  tries to rattle hirata by invoking ayanokoji s abandonment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p222-1\">Depth review: the duel lost<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.222–229<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Faces Hirata in the forest after Class A&#x27;s guard units are split up; outnumbered and without his VIP nearby.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Not bad, Hirata... You&#x27;re way more skilled than I thought.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Never seen you with such a desperate look on your face before!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;That was some serious spirit, Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Guess I pushed the honor student a little too far—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Fights a disciplined close-range duel, uses psychological taunts about Ayanokōji abandoning Hirata, and is eliminated by a slightly faster shot to the chest.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Frank and observant, admits respect for an opponent mid-fight; quick to read the killing intent in Hirata&#x27;s aim.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Loses narrowly to Hirata; is left shaken when Hirata raises the gun again after the match is decided.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Duel opponent; praises his spirit, then fears for his life when the trigger is squeezed partway.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Tries to rattle Hirata by invoking Ayanokōji&#x27;s abandonment.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p221-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Hashimoto&#x27;s duel with Hirata<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p252-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: praise, then a bad feeling<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke depth review  the honor student s restraint engages hashimoto in a close range paintball duel in the forest after class a s gps is jammed  eliminates hashimoto with a slightly faster shot to the chest  fights with  naked killing intent  unbecoming of a mere honor student  driven by resentment over ayanokoji s transfer  after the match is decided  raises the muzzle to hashimoto s forehead and places a finger on the trigger   then stops and walks away without firing  duel opponent  nearly fires a follow up shot at the already eliminated hashimoto  resents being  abandoned  by his transfer   the emotional core of his aggression in this volume  hirata s internal state is shown only through hashimoto s observations  the narration never enters his head  so no direct quote is attributed to him in this duel","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-1\">Depth review: the honor student&#x27;s restraint<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.222–230<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Engages Hashimoto in a close-range paintball duel in the forest after Class A&#x27;s GPS is jammed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Eliminates Hashimoto with a slightly faster shot to the chest.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fights with &quot;naked killing intent, unbecoming of a mere honor student,&quot; driven by resentment over Ayanokōji&#x27;s transfer.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> After the match is decided, raises the muzzle to Hashimoto&#x27;s forehead and places a finger on the trigger — then stops and walks away without firing.<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Duel opponent; nearly fires a follow-up shot at the already-eliminated Hashimoto.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Resents being &quot;abandoned&quot; by his transfer — the emotional core of his aggression in this volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata&#x27;s internal state is shown only through Hashimoto&#x27;s observations; the narration never enters his head, so no direct quote is attributed to him in this duel.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-2\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Hirata&#x27;s killing intent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke year 3  vol  3 ch 7   depth read  hirata s killing intent  not bad  hirata  you re way more skilled than i thought  there s no hesitation or mercy in your aim    hashimoto fights with  naked killing intent  unbecoming of a mere honor student  driven by resentment over ayanokoji s transfer  after defeating hashimoto he raises the gun on the already out opponent but stops before firing  duels him and wins  nearly fires a follow up shot but restrains himself  his anger at being  abandoned  by the transfer fuels his aggression  noted by hashimoto s taunt  hirata s internal state is shown only through hashimoto s observations  no hirata line is quoted in the duel","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-2\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Hirata&#x27;s killing intent<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;Not bad, Hirata... You&#x27;re way more skilled than I thought. There&#x27;s no hesitation or mercy in your aim.&quot; — Hashimoto<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fights with &quot;naked killing intent, unbecoming of a mere honor student,&quot; driven by resentment over Ayanokōji&#x27;s transfer; after defeating Hashimoto he raises the gun on the already-out opponent but stops before firing.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Duels him and wins; nearly fires a follow-up shot but restrains himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His anger at being &quot;abandoned&quot; by the transfer fuels his aggression (noted by Hashimoto&#x27;s taunt).<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata&#x27;s internal state is shown only through Hashimoto&#x27;s observations; no Hirata line is quoted in the duel.<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y3v3-p222-1\">← Before: Depth review: the honor student&#x27;s restraint<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p230-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka shimazaki-ikkei shiraishi-asuka","q":"shiraishi asuka year 3  vol  3 ch 7   depth read  shiraishi reports the chaos  the tactic s effect has worn off and it seems class a s current locations were all displayed at once   just as you said  ayanokouji kun  it s turned into quite a chaotic battle  hasn t it   i imagine class a is surprised right about now   so  they were skillfully outplayed by you alone  ayanokouji kun  calmly relays the battlefield state as recon commander  impressed by ayanokoji s manipulation of all three classes  reports to him and admiration for his outplaying of class a  prepares to use the individual gps shutdown on class d s vips","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p230-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html#sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p230-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Shiraishi reports the chaos<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;The tactic&#x27;s effect has worn off and it seems Class A&#x27;s current locations were all displayed at once.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;Just as you said, Ayanokouji-kun, it&#x27;s turned into quite a chaotic battle, hasn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;I imagine Class A is surprised right about now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, they were skillfully outplayed by you alone, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calmly relays the battlefield state as recon commander; impressed by Ayanokōji&#x27;s manipulation of all three classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.230–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reports to him and admiration for his outplaying of Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.230–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Prepares to use the individual GPS shutdown on Class D&#x27;s VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p160-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.5 — depth read: Class D&#x27;s trust impresses<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p233-1\">→ After: Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: reporting the final state<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio shiina-hiyori beppu-ryouta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  the bluff and the true goal stands over the battlefield as the three minute mark seals class a s elimination  kanzaki  the two class d vips  shiraishi and yamamura gather before him   were the remaining guards taken out   tell me the details   then there are three left  i just took down yoshimoto there a moment ago   it s not robbery or anything  it s just a transfer   i have 22 rounds left  that should be enough   i surrender   impossible  there s no way i can dodge them all   i already told you it s impossible  the muzzle velocity of these paint guns is about 90 m s   it s a matter of perspective   there s nothing in the rules against it   i ll make it official here  i  class d and ichinose have joined forces   that s right  unfortunately for you  winning a shootout wasn t my first priority   it was a matter of sooner or later  burns his ammunition against ibuki and ryuen  eliminates ibuki with a paintball to the thigh  then   out of ammo and apparently surrendered   throws a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on ryuen s abdomen  eliminating both  led ryuen onto the coverless beach and bluffed that yamamura was behind him  exploiting ryuen s need for a certain victory  the damaged paintball was prepared over three days of repeated trials  reveals the exam s true goal  he allowed class b s surprise attack so that cornered class c would have no choice but to request an alliance with class d  class c places second behind class d  the alliance is now open  and a new exam built on trust and betrayal is announced  fights him on the beach  ryuen concedes and vows no mercy from here on  outmaneuvers her in the forest and eliminates her with a paintball to the thigh  looks for her on the disembarkation beach and finds her talking with kaneda  in good spirits  takes the class d vip with him to the center of e11 to bait the confrontation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the bluff and the true goal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands over the battlefield as the three-minute mark seals Class A&#x27;s elimination; Kanzaki, the two Class D VIPs, Shiraishi and Yamamura gather before him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/beppu-ryouta.html\">Beppu Ryōta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Were the remaining guards taken out?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Tell me the details.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Then there are three left. I just took down Yoshimoto there a moment ago.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not robbery or anything. It&#x27;s just a transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have 22 rounds left. That should be enough.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I surrender.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Impossible. There&#x27;s no way I can dodge them all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I already told you it&#x27;s impossible. The muzzle velocity of these paint guns is about 90 m/s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s a matter of perspective.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s nothing in the rules against it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll make it official here. I, Class D and Ichinose have joined forces.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s right. Unfortunately for you, winning a shootout wasn&#x27;t my first priority.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It was a matter of sooner or later.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Burns his ammunition against Ibuki and Ryūen, eliminates Ibuki with a paintball to the thigh, then — out of ammo and apparently surrendered — throws a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on Ryūen&#x27;s abdomen, eliminating both.<span class=\"pg\">p.240–248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Led Ryūen onto the coverless beach and bluffed that Yamamura was behind him, exploiting Ryūen&#x27;s need for a certain victory; the damaged paintball was prepared over three days of repeated trials.<span class=\"pg\">p.245–249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reveals the exam&#x27;s true goal: he allowed Class B&#x27;s surprise attack so that cornered Class C would have no choice but to request an alliance with Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C places second behind Class D; the alliance is now open, and a new exam built on trust and betrayal is announced.<span class=\"pg\">p.251–252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Fights him on the beach; Ryūen concedes and vows no mercy from here on.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Outmaneuvers her in the forest and eliminates her with a paintball to the thigh.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Looks for her on the disembarkation beach and finds her talking with Kaneda, in good spirits.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> Takes the Class D VIP with him to the center of E11 to bait the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.235–236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p202-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: the mastermind&#x27;s final-day moves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p233-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  the guard who relays the map spreads out a map for the breathless yamamura and reports the surviving class b members and their location   the ones left in class b are ryuuen and ibuki  as well as yamashita and yoshimoto  their location is d11   i appreciate it  but doesn t this break the rules   but what about you  do you have enough ammo   then i can t accept this  you should be able to use it more effectively than me  practical and rule conscious   takes charge of the map and intel  and hesitates to accept ayanokoji s spare magazines until he is assured his leader has enough  receives two spare magazines from him to protect the class d vips  protects her class s vips  beppu and himeno  in the final stage","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p233-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the guard who relays the map<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spreads out a map for the breathless Yamamura and reports the surviving Class B members and their location.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;The ones left in Class B are Ryuuen and Ibuki, as well as Yamashita and Yoshimoto. Their location is D11—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;I appreciate it, but doesn&#x27;t this break the rules—?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;But what about you? Do you have enough ammo?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then I can&#x27;t accept this. You should be able to use it more effectively than me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Practical and rule-conscious — takes charge of the map and intel, and hesitates to accept Ayanokōji&#x27;s spare magazines until he is assured his leader has enough.<span class=\"pg\">p.233–234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Receives two spare magazines from him to protect the Class D VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Protects her class&#x27;s VIPs, Beppu and Himeno, in the final stage.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y3v3-p174-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Kanzaki&#x27;s report and debate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p233-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami shiraishi-asuka","q":"shiraishi asuka year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  reporting the final state arrives breathless with yamamura  kanzaki and the two class d vips to report the situation after ayanokoji s solo action   yes  we were attacked by two class b students while we were running away  according to ichinose san  it seems those two had their personal gps signals turned off  so they completely caught us by surprise  recovers from the surprise attack and reports calmly despite being out of breath  confirms the surviving class b members and their location  reports to him  acknowledges his buying them time with his solo action  relays her information about class b s gps jamming attackers","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html#sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p233-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: reporting the final state<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives breathless with Yamamura, Kanzaki and the two Class D VIPs to report the situation after Ayanokōji&#x27;s solo action.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;Yes. We were attacked by two Class B students while we were running away... According to Ichinose-san, it seems those two had their personal GPS signals turned off, so they completely caught us by surprise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Recovers from the surprise attack and reports calmly despite being out of breath; confirms the surviving Class B members and their location.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reports to him; acknowledges his buying them time with his solo action.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Relays her information about Class B&#x27;s GPS-jamming attackers.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiraishi-asuka-y3v3-p230-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.7 — depth read: Shiraishi reports the chaos<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p233-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru yamamura-miki","q":"yamamura miki year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  the unseen final guard arrives out of breath with shiraishi  kanzaki and the two class d vips after ayanokoji s solo action  too exhausted to speak  survives to the final stage as class c s last guard and is named by ayanokoji as the ideal person to sneak up silently   light  nimble and skilled at erasing her presence   which makes the bluff against ryuen credible  is named as the guard who might be positioned behind ryuen  though she was never actually there  is used as a phantom threat to force him to turn around in the final standoff","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamamura-miki.html#sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p233-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the unseen final guard<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives out of breath with Shiraishi, Kanzaki and the two Class D VIPs after Ayanokōji&#x27;s solo action; too exhausted to speak.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Survives to the final stage as Class C&#x27;s last guard and is named by Ayanokōji as the ideal person to sneak up silently — light, nimble and skilled at erasing her presence — which makes the bluff against Ryūen credible.<span class=\"pg\">p.233, 246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is named as the guard who might be positioned behind Ryūen, though she was never actually there.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Is used as a phantom threat to force him to turn around in the final standoff.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamamura-miki-y3v3-p94-1\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.3 — depth read: Yamamura&#x27;s fear and reassurance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-beppu-ryouta-y3v3-p235-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka beppu-ryouta","q":"beppu ryota year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  the vip who walks into the trap is asked by ayanokoji to accompany him to the center of e11 to check the enemy s position and bait the confrontation   what are you going to do   i hope you re right  to be honest  i m at my absolute limit   what s with her  is she a tsundere or something  well  i m outta here  then  exhausted after nearly four days on the island but game   tracks the enemy positions for ayanokoji  then withdraws lightly when ibuki s shout reveals their approach  acts as his spotter and is sent away before the confrontation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-beppu-ryouta-y3v3-p235-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/beppu-ryouta.html#sc-beppu-ryouta-y3v3-p235-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the VIP who walks into the trap<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/beppu-ryouta.html\">Beppu Ryōta<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is asked by Ayanokōji to accompany him to the center of E11 to check the enemy&#x27;s position and bait the confrontation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> &quot;What are you going to do...?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> &quot;I hope you&#x27;re right... To be honest, I&#x27;m at my absolute limit...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> &quot;What&#x27;s with her, is she a tsundere or something...? Well, I&#x27;m outta here, then?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Exhausted after nearly four days on the island but game — tracks the enemy positions for Ayanokōji, then withdraws lightly when Ibuki&#x27;s shout reveals their approach.<span class=\"pg\">p.235–236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Acts as his spotter and is sent away before the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.235–236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p236-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  the wild card falls emerges from the trees beside ryuen to confront ayanokoji in the final shrinking area   die  ayanokouji   where are you even aiming  you think you re gonna hit me with a shot that pathetic  you re a lousy shot   agh  dammit  so this is how it ends  this is so fucking annoying  i told you i didn t want to do this  suppresses ayanokoji with a submachine gun spray and runs between the trees with animal like speed  but is eliminated by a paintball to the right thigh when she misreads his aim  ferocious and impatient   relishes the frontal fight  taunts her opponent  and rages at being eliminated in a game she never wanted to play  is outmaneuvered and eliminated by him  ryuen reveals she had wanted to gamble everything on a shot at a class d vip rather than the 2 v 1","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p236-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the wild card falls<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Emerges from the trees beside Ryūen to confront Ayanokōji in the final shrinking area.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Die, Ayanokouji!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Where are you even aiming? You think you&#x27;re gonna hit me with a shot that pathetic? You&#x27;re a lousy shot.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Agh, dammit! So this is how it ends!? This is so fucking annoying!! I told you I didn&#x27;t want to do this!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Suppresses Ayanokōji with a submachine-gun spray and runs between the trees with animal-like speed, but is eliminated by a paintball to the right thigh when she misreads his aim.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ferocious and impatient — relishes the frontal fight, taunts her opponent, and rages at being eliminated in a game she never wanted to play.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is outmaneuvered and eliminated by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen reveals she had wanted to gamble everything on a shot at a Class D VIP rather than the 2-v-1.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p131-1\">← Before: Depth review: the wild card eliminated<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p236-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  the duel lost  defeat conceded emerges from the trees with ibuki and yamashita to confront ayanokoji in the shrinking center of e11   sounds like you were pretty successful  how many people did you take out   i don t like it  but it s thanks to the information you sent  a convergence of interests  i suppose   yeah  but i d like to hand you a loss just as much  time s running out  let s settle this here and now and decide our ranks   so even you can t dodge every bullet here  can you   gotta take every precaution when i m up against you  ayanokouji  right   even in a 2 v 1  there s no guarantee we d win a shootout against you   nah  if it were just about winning  i d have thought that was the better move  too   i just wanna know  is this really you surrendering   no matter who you are  there s no way you can dodge every single bullet i fire  right   you  threw it   in the end  that idiot ibuki was the most right  huh   i ve seen your process of using any environment to win  in that case  from here on out  i m not gonna show you any mercy in the truest sense  cornered ayanokoji on the beach with an overwhelming ammunition advantage but lost when the damaged paintball burst on his abdomen  accepts the defeat with a declaration of future  merciless rivalry  driven by obsession with a certain victory   refuses the safe all or nothing shot at a vip and insists on beating ayanokoji directly  even at the risk of his own defeat  fights him on the beach  concedes defeat  and vows no mercy from here on  says her preference was to gamble on an all or nothing shot at a vip rather than challenge ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p236-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: the duel lost, defeat conceded<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Emerges from the trees with Ibuki and Yamashita to confront Ayanokōji in the shrinking center of E11.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Sounds like you were pretty successful. How many people did you take out?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t like it, but it&#x27;s thanks to the information you sent. A convergence of interests, I suppose?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Yeah. But I&#x27;d like to hand you a loss just as much. Time&#x27;s running out. Let&#x27;s settle this here and now and decide our ranks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So even you can&#x27;t dodge every bullet here, can you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Gotta take every precaution when I&#x27;m up against you, Ayanokouji, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even in a 2-v-1, there&#x27;s no guarantee we&#x27;d win a shootout against you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nah. If it were just about winning, I&#x27;d have thought that was the better move, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I just wanna know, is this really you surrendering?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No matter who you are, there&#x27;s no way you can dodge every single bullet I fire, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You... threw it...!?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In the end, that idiot Ibuki was the most right, huh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ve seen your process of using any environment to win. In that case, from here on out, I&#x27;m not gonna show you any mercy in the truest sense.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Cornered Ayanokōji on the beach with an overwhelming ammunition advantage but lost when the damaged paintball burst on his abdomen; accepts the defeat with a declaration of future, merciless rivalry.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Driven by obsession with a certain victory — refuses the safe all-or-nothing shot at a VIP and insists on beating Ayanokōji directly, even at the risk of his own defeat.<span class=\"pg\">p.241–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Fights him on the beach, concedes defeat, and vows no mercy from here on.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Says her preference was to gamble on an all-or-nothing shot at a VIP rather than challenge Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y3v3-p172-2\">← Before: Year 3, Vol. 3 Ch.6 — depth read: Ryūen through Shiina<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p251-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kaneda-satoru shiina-hiyori","q":"shiina hiyori year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  found in good spirits is not seen once during the island exam  on the disembarkation beach ayanokoji spots her in the distance talking with kaneda  appears uninjured and in good spirits  continuing the reconciliation begun in the library   a quiet sign of the friends she has made  is searched for by him after the exam  he wonders whether to go over but is swept up by yoshida and hashimoto  is seen talking with him on the beach","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p251-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html#sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p251-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: found in good spirits<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is not seen once during the island exam; on the disembarkation beach Ayanokōji spots her in the distance talking with Kaneda.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Appears uninjured and in good spirits, continuing the reconciliation begun in the library — a quiet sign of the friends she has made.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is searched for by him after the exam; he wonders whether to go over but is swept up by Yoshida and Hashimoto.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Is seen talking with him on the beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y3v3-p172-1\">← Before: Depth review: beach conversation with Ryūen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p252-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yoshida-kenta hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi year 3  vol  3 epilogue   depth read  praise  then a bad feeling  man  don t you get a really bad feeling about this  comes to praise ayanokoji for the second place finish  then   with yoshida   senses the strange  solemn atmosphere of the results announcement before the new exam is revealed  congratulates him on the result and shares his unease  celebrates second place with him at the disembarkation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p252-1\">Year 3, Vol. 3 Epilogue — depth read: praise, then a bad feeling<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · <\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Man, don&#x27;t you get a really bad feeling about this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Comes to praise Ayanokōji for the second-place finish, then — with Yoshida — senses the strange, solemn atmosphere of the results announcement before the new exam is revealed.<span class=\"pg\">p.251–252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Congratulates him on the result and shares his unease.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Celebrates second place with him at the disembarkation.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y3v3-p222-1\">← Before: Depth review: the duel lost<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
